\ Exact direct count after every month has appeared at least once.
\ Once all months have started, the first-occurrence condition is
\ satisfied forever. Only the order of their FINAL occurrences remains.
\
\ In any unfinished suffix, list positive remaining counts of months
\ in increasing original month order as r1,r2,...,rk.
\ S_j = r1+...+r_j.
\ The number of completions whose last occurrences retain the order
\ 1,2,...,k is exactly:
\   product(j=1..k) C(S_j-1,r_j-1).
\
\ Proof: reverse each completed suffix. The final-occurrence condition
\ becomes first-appearance order k,k-1,...,1. Among permutations of a
\ multiset the first NEW symbol follows size-biased ordering; the
\ probability for that prescribed order is
\   product(j=k..2) r_j/S_j.
\ Multiplication by the multinomial coefficient simplifies into the
\ integer binomial product above. The formula remains valid with any
\ earlier months already fully exhausted.
\
\ This shortcut works with arbitrarily many previously started months.
\ It needs NO recursive calls, NO memo entries and NO nested loops.
\ The binomial coefficient calculator preserves arbitrary precision.
\ The shortcut never applies if even one month has not yet started.
\ CAL compilation and execution remain unverified.

A started weaving suffix has
  a number called available,
  a number called accumulated remaining,
  a number called binomial top,
  a number called binomial bottom,
  a wide quantity called completions.

The started weaving suffix is a started weaving suffix.
The started weaving month is a woven month state.

To count an all-started weaving suffix:
  Put 0 into the started weaving suffix's available.
  Inspect the woven month status.
  If the weaving selection's already started is not the selected month count, exit.
  Put 1 into the started weaving suffix's available.
  Put 0 into the started weaving suffix's accumulated remaining.
  Put "1" into the started weaving suffix's completions.
  Put the woven month states' first into the started weaving month.
  Loop.
    If the started weaving month is nil, break.
    If the started weaving month's remaining days is greater than 0,
      accumulate the started weaving month.
    Put the started weaving month's next into the started weaving month.
  Repeat.

\ For one unfinished month this factor is C(r-1,r-1) = 1.
\ Later factors preserve the exact last-occurrence ordering.
To accumulate the started weaving month:
  Put the started weaving suffix's accumulated remaining into the started weaving suffix's binomial top.
  Add the started weaving month's remaining days to the started weaving suffix's binomial top.
  Subtract 1 from the started weaving suffix's binomial top.
  Put the started weaving month's remaining days into the started weaving suffix's binomial bottom.
  Subtract 1 from the started weaving suffix's binomial bottom.
  Calculate a binomial coefficient given the started weaving suffix's binomial top and the started weaving suffix's binomial bottom.
  Multiply the binomial result by the started weaving suffix's completions.
  Add the started weaving month's remaining days to the started weaving suffix's accumulated remaining.
